lisa-design:
- Security settings owned by an ENFORCED org code security configuration (value enabled/disabled, not not_set) are skipped without reading the repo value: the org config is authoritative and GitHub 422s any repo-level write. Matching -> Plan.Managed line; differing -> Plan.Warnings (counted, never fails the run).
- Generalised to both Dependabot settings (vulnerability_alerts <-> dependabot_alerts, dependabot_security_updates), since the same 422 applies to both; the spec only named security updates.
- GET code-security-configuration: 404/403/204 and detached/removed statuses = no configuration (403 isn't surfaced; a later 422 is still reported as a failed step).
- SecurityUpdates returns *bool: nil (403 or missing "enabled") = unknown -> Plan.Unknown, and Apply writes the desired value, mirroring the merge-settings unknown handling. 404 stays "disabled" (GitHub's documented meaning: Dependabot off).
- Apply returns []StepResult and never aborts; order is merge, rulesets, vulnerability alerts, security updates (the refusable writes last). Run prints per-step failures + "applied N step(s)"/"partly applied: F of N step(s) failed" and returns errors.Join, so main still exits 1.
- The original misread was not a defaulting bug: the old code decoded enabled as a plain bool (absent -> false) and treated 404 as false, so GitHub actually returned enabled:true at plan time; the org config's updated_at (23:06:48Z) is 35s before the run, so propagation of a just-changed enforced config is the likely cause. Skipping enforced settings makes the tool independent of that.
